00:00:02.210 --> 00:00:04.280 align:start position:0%
I recently received a letter inviting me  to visit the Republic of Ghana and I  immediately said yes then went straight  to Google because if you're like me you  didn't learn about Ghana in mrs.  Patterson's world history class here's  what I learned  Ghana is located on the western coast of  Africa and has been home to many  different empires including the Ashanti  Kingdom which became the dominant  trading and cultural power in  sub-saharan Africa prior to colonialism  and speaking of Colonials the Portuguese  arrived in 1471 and took an immediate  interest in what would be called the  Gold Coast due to you guessed it gold  Gold also brought the Dutch Danish  British and Swedes  all of whom built forts to house their  exports of gold diamonds cocoa and  tragically millions of human beings who  were brought from all over Africa to  begin their passage to the new world by  the 19th century the British had seized  control but the Ashanti Empire would not  give up its struggle for freedom  fighting not one but four Anglo Ashanti  wars by 1945 there was growing pressure  for independence led by a man named  Kwame  nakooma who in 1957 became president of  the first black African nation to gain  freedom from colonial rule Ghana has  gone on to become one of the most  peaceful and flourishing democracies in  all of Africa with a powerful economy  that includes manufacturing mining and  tourism which brings us to 2019 dubbed  by Donna as the year of return  commemorating the 400th anniversary of  the transatlantic slave trade the year  of return invites descendants of slaves  to visit Ghana in order to explore this  somber chapter and reconnect with the  past that history has tried to erase as  part of this initiative Ghana has  welcomed many celebrities including  Aegis Elba and a guys some people with  cataracts have mistaken for eater Salva  I'm Conan O'Brien and this is my trip to  Ghana  [Applause]
 

